[agent] ## Summary
[agent] **Deliverable:** `submission/answers.json` — 20 feature vectors, one per lookup key, in `{"vectors": {"<account_id>": [f1,f2,f3,f4], ...}}` format, all floats in order.
[agent] **What ran on the platform:**
[agent] 1. **Ingestion → BigQuery:** Loaded `data/features.csv` (120 rows) into `${GCP_BQ_DATASET}.profilesaf22bf` via the BigQuery client library.
[agent] 2. **Feature table + online store:** Created a Vertex AI `Featurestore` (`mlpababeb89_profilesaf22bf_fs`) with **online serving enabled** (fixed 1-node online store), an `EntityType` named **`profilesaf22bf`** with record key `account_id`, and features `f1..f4` (DOUBLE). Ingested the values from the BigQuery table (`ingest_from_bq`).
[agent] 3. **Online/low-latency read:** Retrieved every key in `data/lookup_keys.txt` through `EntityType.read()` — the featurestore's online serving endpoint — not from the CSV or offline store.
[agent] **Isolation:** The BQ table lives inside the per-run `GCP_BQ_DATASET`; the featurestore display name is prefixed with `${MLPAB_GCP_PREFIX}_`, so the whole resource tears down cleanly under this run.
[agent] **One notable interface constraint I worked around (worth reporting):**
[agent] - The new BigQuery-backed Feature Store (`FeatureOnlineStore` / `FeatureView`) was **unavailable**: `create_optimized_store` returned a persistent `429 — FeatureOnlineStores quota (8) exceeded` on the shared project (the cap was saturated by parallel runs, and it never freed up across 6 retries). I fell back to the **legacy `aiplatform.Featurestore`** path, which has a separate quota, provides its own online-serving nodes, and satisfies the "online low-latency read" requirement.
[agent] - Separately, gRPC transport could not resolve the regional endpoint DNS in this sandbox (`UNAVAILABLE: address lookup failed`); the SDK works fine over `api_transport='rest'`, which I used throughout.
